# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/

# Training outputs (regenerable: checkpoints, per-run snapshots, plots).
# Keep models/.gitkeep so the directory stays in the tree.
/models/*
!/models/.gitkeep

# Run logs (train/eval/probe stdout). Regenerable and huge — a 500k-trial training log is
# ~10 MB of "Trial n/N".
*.log

# RUN RESULTS ARE NEVER COMMITTED — no exceptions, including probe logs. Harness stdout is
# not repo content; the numbers that matter get transcribed into RESEARCH_LOG.md, which IS the
# record. What stays tracked is the *code that produces* a result (/runs/, probe.py, r6_accept.py)
# and the *write-up that interprets* it (probes/*.md, RESEARCH_LOG.md) — never the stdout itself.
#
# History, so the drift is not repeated: three *_results.txt sat tracked at the repo root, not
# by decision but because the old rule ignored only ROOT-level *.log while nothing ignored root
# *.txt, so `git add` swept them in. probes/*.log were tracked by an explicit older decision
# ("deliberate artefacts of a probe write-up"); that decision is REVERSED as of 2026-07-19.
#
# NOTE: RESEARCH_LOG.md and probes/*.md cite some probe logs by filename. Those files remain on
# disk locally but are no longer in the repo, so a fresh clone will not have them — the citation
# names the run that produced a number, it is not a promise the file is in the tree.
/results/
*_results.txt
code_review*.txt
